<title>USA: San Antonio feeder cattle steady-up $2 - USDA.</title>
<headline>San Antonio feeder cattle steady-up $2 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers were steady to $2.00 per cwt higher and feeder heifers were steady to firm, compared to last week, USDA said.</p>
<p>Trade was active and demand good. Bulk of supply Medium and Large 1-2 600-900 lb feeder steers and heifers. Supply included around 8 percent slaughter cows and bulls, 45 percent feeder cattle over 600 lbs with balance mostly feeder cattle under 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs 78.00-83.00, pkg 622 lbs 85.50; 700-800 lbs 73.00-77.50; 800-900 lbs 70.75-77.75. Medium and Large 1-2 - few 300-400 lbs 87.00-89.00; few 400-500 lb 82.50-86.00; few 500-600 lb 78.00-81.00; few 600-700 lbs 75.00-79.00; few 700-800 lbs 70.00-72.00.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs 73.00-77.50; 700-800 lbs 69.25- 74.75. Medium and Large 1-2 - 600-700 lbs 68.50-72.75; 700-800 lbs 65.25-70.00.</p>
<p>Cattle and Calves - 1,575  Last week- 1,349  Last Year- 2,364</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
